D:1218\", source=\"MESH:D004451/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:124169:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:7457\", source=\"ICD10CM:B80\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:124459:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:1217\", source=\"MESH:D005213/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:124972:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:11379\", source=\"ICD10CM:B83.1/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D058429/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:125531:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:10074\", source=\"ICD10CM:B71.0/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D006925/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:127539:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:2790\", source=\"ICD10CM:B76.1/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D009332/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:127566:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"MESH:D009349\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:127751:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:3983\", source=\"MESH:D009814/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:127836:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:13768\", source=\"ICD10CM:B66.0/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D009889/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:128175:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:10699\", source=\"ICD10CM:B66.4/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D010237/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:129657:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:10080\", source=\"ICD10CM:B70.1/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D013031/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:129955:def: \"An infection that is caused by nematodes of the genus Strongyloides, most commonly Strongyloides stercoralis, which is a soil-transmitted helminth, and which is characterized by a variety of gastrointestinal, dermatologic, and, occasionally, pulmonary manifestations. The worm's autoinfective life cycle can lead to hyper-infection and life-threatening dissemination in immunocompromised hosts decades after initial infection.\" [NCIT:C128398]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:129989:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:10955\", source=\"MESH:D013322/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:130309:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:3107\", source=\"MESH:D017227/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:130348:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:9790\", source=\"MESH:D014120/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:130518:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:1255\", source=\"MESH:D014252/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:130552:def: \"An infection that is caused by the nematode Trichuris trichiura, a soil-transmitted helminth, which is transmitted via food and/or water contaminated with the eggs of the worm. Symptoms are usually mild and include abdominal pain, diarrhea, fatigue, and possibly anemia secondary to blood loss in diarrhea.\" [NCIT:C128399]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:130577:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:1252\", source=\"ICD10CM:B79\", source=\"MESH:D014257/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:150049:is_a: MONDO:7770006 ! disease by body system or component\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:209175:comment: Diagnosis of CF requires **one clinical indicator** (positive newborn screen, symptoms consistent with CF, or family history) **plus one functional/genetic indicator**:\\n1. Sweat chloride concentration ≥60 mmol/L, or\\n2. Identification of two CF-causing CFTR pathogenic variants, or\\n3. Abnormal nasal potential difference measurement\\n\\nSee also CFTR-related disorders (MONDO:7770004), which involve CFTR dysfunction limited to a single organ system and do not meet CF diagnostic criteria.\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:217017:comment: Created new term for GTP Cyclohydrolase I deficiency with hyperphenylalaninemia and created grouping class named GTP Cyclohydrolase I deficiency. Obsoleted this to avoid confusion with the new grouping class and the class this was renamed to.\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:221126:comment: This term represents both \"hereditary\" and \"non-hereditary\" multiple intestinal atresia. It is generally accepted to not distinguish the non-hereditary concept, and use the term \"multiple intestinal atresia\" to refer to non-hereditary multiple intestinal atresia (PMID:33674188). Since this distinction is not necessary, we have not created a specific term for \"non-hereditary multiple intestinal atresia\". However, if the need arises, a new term can be added to Mondo to represent this concept. This term's classification was reviewed in the context of the Strategic Refinement project (2023) and was determined to be excluded from the 'immune system disorder' (MONDO:0005046) ontology branch (https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8216-5084).\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:226375:comment: Split this into a new term, this term had both a OMIMPS and OMIM class as equivalent.\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:230183:synonym: \"hereditary sensory and autonomic neuropathy caused by mutation in NTRK1\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:230190:synonym: \"NTRK1 hereditary sensory and autonomic neuropathy\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:230208:intersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8031 ! NTRK1\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:230210:relationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8031 {source=\"OMIM:256800\"} ! NTRK1\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:242909:is_a: MONDO:7770004 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! CFTR-related disorder\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:333516:relationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8032 {source=\"OMIM:613886\"} ! NTRK2\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:338571:comment: Replaced this term with a new term with a new label.\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:379289:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:7033\", source=\"ICD10CM:B81.0/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D017129/inferred\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:380496:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:1395\", source=\"MESH:D012552/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:380615:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:10075\", source=\"ICD10CM:B70.0/inferred\", source=\"MESH:D004169/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:395321:comment: Moved Orphanet equiv dbxref to parent class (glioma). Therefore obsoleted this term and created a new term that is not equiv to Orphanet:182067.\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:398829:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:1080\", source=\"ICD10CM:B74\", source=\"MESH:D005368/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:413130:synonym: \"ETANTR\" RELATED ABBREVIATION [GARD:0006352, ONCOTREE:ETANTR]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:413143:xref: ONCOTREE:ETANTR {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:465055:is_a: MONDO:7770009 ! disease of genetic or genomic mechanism\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:466881:is_a: MONDO:7770011 ! disease by molecular mechanism\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:467525:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:0050256\", source=\"MESH:C536369/inferred\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:468026:def: \"Tropical endomyocardial fibrosis is a restrictive cardiopathy, occurring almost exclusively in children and young adults in tropical and subtropical regions, characterized by endocardial fibrosis, affecting the apices and the inflow tract of the right or left ventricle (or both) and manifesting with a restrictive cardimyopathy and atrioventricular regurgitation leading to severe pulmonary hypertension, very high systemic venous pressure and congestive cardiac failure. Suspected etiologies include helminth and protozoal infestation and malnutrition.\" [Orphanet:75565]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:471638:is_a: MONDO:7770007 ! disease by developmental or physiological process\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:475426:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"DOID:9784\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:506075:is_a: MONDO:7770011 ! disease by molecular mechanism\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:508037:is_a: MONDO:7770007 ! disease by developmental or physiological process\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:508340:is_a: MONDO:7770007 ! disease by developmental or physiological process\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:508599:is_a: MONDO:7770011 ! disease by molecular mechanism\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:516802:is_a: MONDO:7770010 ! disease of primarily extrinsic mechanism\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:519330:synonym: \"NEOPL CERVICAL INTRAEPITHELIAL\" RELATED [MESH:D018290]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:526680:name: intestinal helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:526681:def: \"A parasitic helminthiasis infectious disease that involves the intestine.\" [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:526683:synonym: \"intestine parasitic helminthiasis infectious disease\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:526688:is_a: MONDO:0004664 {source=\"MESH:C531698\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\"} ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:526690:intersection_of: MONDO:0004664 ! helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:527493:is_a: MONDO:7770007 ! disease by developmental or physiological process\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:528679:is_a: MONDO:7770006 ! disease by body system or component\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:531447:is_a: MONDO:7770006 ! disease by body system or component\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:533574:name: helminthiasis, animal\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:533575:def: \"Infestation of animals with parasitic worms of the helminth class. The infestation may be experimental or veterinary.\" [MESH:D006374]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:533576:synonym: \"animal Helminthiases\" RELATED [MESH:D006374]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:533577:synonym: \"animal helminthiasis\" RELATED [MESH:D006374]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:533578:synonym: \"Helminthiases, animal\" RELATED [MESH:D006374]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:533582:intersection_of: MONDO:0700097 MONDO:0004664 ! cross-species analog helminthiasis\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:533925:is_a: MONDO:0025082 {source=\"MESH:D013319\"} ! helminthiasis, animal\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:536444:is_a: MONDO:7770010 ! disease of primarily extrinsic mechanism\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:537822:synonym: \"PERIVENTRICULAR NODULAR HETEROTOPIA 9\" EXACT [DOID:0061246, OMIM:618918]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:537844:synonym: \"ARRHYTHMOGENIC RIGHT VENTRICULAR DYSPLASIA, FAMILIAL, 14\" EXACT [OMIM:618920]\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:553293:relationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8032 {source=\"OMIM:617830\"} ! NTRK2\nsrc/ontology/mondo-edit.obo:562533:def: \"Infections with true tapeworms of the helminth subclass Cestoda.\" [MESH:D002590]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
